      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of GaussianAvatar. Given a fitted SMPL or SMPL-X model on the current frame, we sample the points on its surface and record their positions on a UV positional map I, which is then passed to a pose encoder to obtain the pose feature. An optimizable feature tensor is pixel-aligned with the pose feature and learned to capture the coarse appearance of humans. Then the two aligned feature tensors are input into the Gaussian parameter decoder, which predicts each point's offset ∆ˆx, color ˆc, and scale ˆ s. These predictions, along with the fixed rotations q and opacity α, collectively constitute the animatable 3D Gaussians in canonical space.",
